º Known limitations                                                         º
ÓÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ½

    ş Supports  2,000 conferences in the shareware version
    ş Supports 10,000 conferences in the professional version
    ş 64k length of messages (standard FTSC)
    ş Requires the HMB to at least be present, even if not used

    Multiboard is  dedicated to making OLMS the premium offline mail
    system.   In the short time that OLMS has been available, it has
    demonstrated the features, support, attention and stability that
    is required on todays high-paced bulletin board systems.


ÖÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ·
º Professional version vs. Shareware version                                º
ÓÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ½

    There are three main visable differences between  the shareware and
    professional versions of OLMS.

    The professional version supports 10,000 message conferences, comes
    with a fancy user editor, and supports vacation mail for your users
    What isn't quite so evident is the 3rd indexing system that is used
    in the professional version.   With the increase of mail areas that
    todays busy BBS's have, many mail doors can seem slow and sluggish,
    particularly when entering the door. With OLMS's use of a 3rd index
    these programs are no longer existant.    On systems,  particularly
    LAN systems,  a substansial speed increase  is visable  with 400 or
    more message areas,  and becomes a  greater increase as your system
    grows in size.

    Also,  the professional version lets  you  tune the number of areas
    you wish to support,  giving you the option of adjusting the size &
    speed of OLMS to tailor directly to your system.

    One other added feature that is quite  nice is  the ability to have
    files  that are  attached to messages,  directly packed without the
    need to request them from your reader after the inital download.

    Many, if not most, systems will not require the additional power of
    the "pro" version, however for the extra few dollars that it costs,
    it might be a valuble investment for the future of your BBS.

